  "interpretation": {
    "strongest_supported_conclusions": [
      "Fixed-size shared framing is not a universal optimum; file-aware/adaptive representations remove tiny-file penalties.",
      "Content-addressed deduplication, sparse/link fidelity, microblocks and exact nested-container handling can create large wins that ordinary per-entry ZIP cannot obtain without additional semantics.",
      "Already-compressed/random workloads require graceful RAW/direct-storage behavior rather than blind recompression.",
      "Durability, integrity and metadata semantics must be made equivalent before comparing timings.",
      "CMPCT architecture demonstrated both size and speed advantages on multiple heterogeneous corpora, but no universal dominance claim is justified until controlled CI and broader independent benchmarking exist."
    ],
    "not_supported_yet": [
      "A claim that CMPCT is universally smaller/faster than every existing archive format.",
      "Public marketing claims based solely on these chat-local development measurements.",
      "Cross-platform production reliability before conformance vectors, fuzzing and native implementation work are completed."
    ]
  }
